 "headline": {
  "pathway": "block9 ell=4 -> (regenerated across blocks 10-11 via tensor-product coupling) -> ell=1 sector of the pre-final-norm state (after block 11) -> force head (narrow(1,0,4))",
  "site11_ell1_rescue_is_structural": "R=1.0000 (to fp32 precision) at site 11 for ell=1-only and ell={0,1}-joint restoration, for both tiers and both alpha values. This is expected by construction (not a discovery): the force head only reads node_embedding.narrow(1,0,4)=l0+l1, and NORM_FIXED already fixes the RMS statistic to baseline, so patching l0+l1 (or l1 alone, since l0 patching alone gives R=0.0000 -- force output does not depend on l0) exactly reconstructs the baseline force. The informative result is upstream of this: how the block-9 ell=4 damage arrives at that l=1 sector by the time it reaches site 11.",
  "site10_partial_rescue_is_the_real_finding": "At site 10 (one block upstream of the force-relevant site), restoring ell=1 alone only recovers R~=0.44-0.46 (LOW) / R~=0.15-0.20 (HIGH) of the damage, while restoring ell=4 alone (the localization control) recovers MORE: R~=0.71-0.76 (LOW) / R~=0.67-0.77 (HIGH). Restoring the original high-order signal before block 11 processes it rescues more than directly overwriting the low-order sector block 11 will read -- block 11 itself performs substantial ell=4 -> ell=1 tensor-product conversion that a site-10 l=1-only patch cannot substitute for."
 },
 "full_population_confirmation": {
  "run": false,
  "reason": "The headline site-11 ell=1 rescue is exact (R=1.0000 to fp32 precision, deterministic paired per-config evaluation) at M=1024 for both tiers and both alpha values -- not power-limited, so a full-27,697 confirmation would not change this conclusion. The scientifically informative site-10 partial-rescue numbers are consistent in sign and magnitude across tier x alpha (4 independent cells each for the ell=1 and ell=4 comparisons), which is the same evidentiary bar used to accept Stage-3's own M=1024 dose-response result before its optional full-population confirmation. Skipped per the task's 'quick' scope; can be added on request."
 }
}